      "category": "authority",
      "symbols": [
        {
          "symbol": "SmartSigner.SignAsync",
          "path": "Acme.Net.Sdk.Signing",
          "signature": "build a signed envelope WITHOUT submitting"
        },
        {
          "symbol": "SmartSigner.SignExistingAsync",
          "path": "Acme.Net.Sdk.Signing",
          "signature": "(Dictionary<string, object?> envelope) -> Task<Dictionary<string, object?>>"
        },
        {
          "symbol": "AccumulateV3Client.SubmitAsync",
          "path": "Acme.Net.Sdk.Signing",
          "signature": "submit the fully-signed envelope"
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "name": "operation",
          "type": "str",
          "required": true,
          "description": "Transaction to run under the threshold, e.g. create_data_account"
        },
        {
          "name": "additionalSigners",
          "type": "list",
          "required": true,
          "description": "Distinct keys that must ALSO sign the SAME transaction"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "txHash",
          "type": "str"
        }
      ],
      "requires": [
        "keypair",
        "credits"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Satisfies an M-of-N signature threshold. Sign once, then co-sign the resulting envelope with each additional key, then submit ONCE.",
        "Signing the same body twice does NOT work: the first signature metadata becomes the transaction initiator and is baked into the header, so a second independent signature is over a different transaction hash and neither copy reaches the threshold.",
        "Collect every signature before submitting \u2014 resubmitting a signature already on chain trips replay protection."
      ],
      "examples": [
        "examples/v3/Example15_CoSigning/Program.cs"
      ]
    },
